"""One-time continuity update; full per-species report is generated separately."""
from pathlib import Path
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
heading='## Global marine fish animation audit — playable v4.0.3, 2026-10-16\n\n'
summary='Audited all 94 registered marine fish, including five acquisition-held clownfish and one fictional fish. Thirty-one have authored adult cycles; 63 previously translated static living poses. Added render-only species profiles, pixel-preserving tail/outer-fin motion, state-aware timing, banked side-profile turns and head/eye protection across three stages. No new biological species, AI/feeding/breeding rules, inheritance or saves are introduced. All 94 remain conservatively classed B (partial) because bespoke action/turn/pectoral artwork and anatomy approvals remain incomplete; this is not a claim of fully authored animation. See [FISH_ANIMATION_AUDIT.md](FISH_ANIMATION_AUDIT.md), [FISH_ANIMATION_SYSTEM.md](FISH_ANIMATION_SYSTEM.md) and [offline motion review](fish-animation-review.html).\n\n'
p=r/'MASTER_DEVELOPMENT_PROMPT.md';old=p.read_text(encoding='utf8');assert 'VERSION 4.5' in old
new=old.replace('VERSION 4.5','VERSION 4.6',1).replace('playable v4.0.2, 2026-10-16','playable v4.0.3, 2026-10-16',1)
new=new.replace('## Ocean diving destination artwork',heading+summary+'## Ocean diving destination artwork',1)
rule='''## 3.14 Global saltwater fish animation — v4.0.3 permanent

Every implemented marine fish must be audited against the runtime roster, with stable biological ID, science/name, real source assets, stages, frame counts, native facing/eyes, dead art and current animation status. Designer morphs are varieties, not extra species. Reference-only subjects are category E and cannot become gameplay livestock through an art change. Preserve all earlier acquisition/anatomy approvals and holds. Maintain FISH_ANIMATION_AUDIT.md with honest A–E classifications; an adult-only swim cycle is not complete lifecycle/action animation.

The presentation authority is AL.FishAnimation, with explicit species/family/stage definitions in assets/animation/fish-registry.json Preserve the current 2D Canvas renderer, original dedicated sprites, approved benchmark, inheritance and head/core markings. Use loaded authored adult clownfish cycles intact; other stages/species can use restrained integer-pixel tail/outer-fin articulation, fixed roots, protected head/eye pixels, transparent padding and nearest-neighbor sampling. Do not replace dedicated fish with generic geometry or fabricate hidden pectoral clean plates. Keep missing authored action/turn/anatomy art explicitly partial until delivered and reviewed.

Idle/hover, normal/fast travel, banked side-profile turns, actual Eat, Rest/Hide, existing nest/guard/courtship/spawning/mouthbrood labels and existing visible health conditions drive artistic motion timing. Distinguish respiratory activity from weak/injured motion. Use only actual diets, health and autonomous breeding state; rendering never initiates feeding, disease, mating or an external brood. Supported Banggai release uses its existing developed-juvenile pose rather than a historical yolk-sac larva. Normalized source direction and sampled existing eyes must survive both facings without an added eye. Persistent death art freezes active fins/posture and retains the simulation's sinking/loss record.

All animation clocks/turn interpolation belong to renderer-owned records; no save fields or biological RNG are consumed. Apply individual patterns before articulation and preserve them through save/load. Reuse final-size rasters and bounded pose caches, avoid per-frame image loading/readback, reuse sort/hit arrays and cull offscreen marine sprite work. Keep click identity aligned with articulated bounds; the three-real-second selection highlight and persistent inspector are unchanged. Check all current species/stages/both directions and representative states, high counts, rendering-rate independence, death, offline saves, protected freshwater differential output and served DIST. A newly added marine species needs an explicit profile and coverage; missing assignments must be reported, not silently counted complete. See FISH_ANIMATION_SYSTEM.md for architecture and current limitations.

'''
assert '# 4. WORLD STRUCTURE' in new;new=new.replace('# 4. WORLD STRUCTURE',rule+'# 4. WORLD STRUCTURE',1);p.write_text(new,encoding='utf8')
p=r/'PROJECT_CONTINUITY_SOURCE.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8');assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new,1).replace('Playable v4.0.2 / MDP v4.5','Playable v4.0.3 / MDP v4.6',1);pos=s.index('\n\n');s=s[:pos+2]+heading+summary+s[pos+2:];p.write_text(s,encoding='utf8')
for name in ['ART_DIRECTION.md','DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md','CURRENT_LIVESTOCK_CATALOG.md','UI_SPECIFICATION.md','README.md','GAME_DESIGN.md','TEST_REPORT.md','GITHUB_PAGES_BUILD_REPORT.md']:
 p=r/name;s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8');pos=s.index('\n\n');s=s[:pos+2]+heading+summary+s[pos+2:];p.write_text(s,encoding='utf8')
p=r/'index.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8');assert 'v4.0.2' in s;p.write_text(s.replace('v4.0.2','v4.0.3'),encoding='utf8')
p=r/'tests/package.py';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8');s=s.replace("'location-art-evidence']","'location-art-evidence','fish-animation-evidence']",1);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf8')
print('Master v4.6 / playable v4.0.3 continuity updated')
